 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for realtime delivery.** Committed changes are pushed to browsers through self-hosted WebSockets rather than HTTPS polling or a hosted realtime service. Accepts operational complexity (connection management, reconnect handling) to achieve subsecond updates without vendor coupling. See [docs/decisions/realtime-delivery-approach.md](../decisions/realtime-delivery-approach.md) for the full analysis.
